  "sn35.245:6.1": "Literally, a “what’s it” tree—apparently, <i>Butea frondosa,</i> the flame of the forest. It is often the subject of riddles in its native habitats because its seasonal changes—such as losing all its leaves just before its striking red flowers bloom—are so vivid and unusual.",
